The '''2026 UEFA Super Cup''' was the 51st edition of the [[UEFA Super Cup]], an annual [[association football|football]] match organised by [[UEFA]] and contested by the reigning champions of the top two European club competitions, the [[UEFA Champions League]] and the [[UEFA Europa League]]. The match featured French club [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]], the winners of the [[2025–26 UEFA Champions League]] and reigning UEFA Super Cup title holders, and English club [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]], the winners of the [[2025–26 UEFA Europa League]]. It was played at the [[Red Bull Arena (Salzburg)|Red Bull Arena]] in [[Salzburg]], Austria,<ref name="ExCo decision"/> on 12 August 2026.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/029d-1ea02fc38447-640d13cb2154-1000/20250901_circular_2025_49_en.zip |title=Men's international match calendar and access list for the 2026/27 season |number=49/2025 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=[[UEFA|Union of European Football Associations]] |format=ZIP |date=2 September 2025 |access-date=11 September 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/02a8-2149ed5e5bc1-0b130f0cdccd-1000--paris-vs-aston-villa-super-cup-preview-where-to-watch-ki/|title=Paris vs Aston Villa Super Cup preview: Where to watch, kick-off time, predicted line-ups|date=11 August 2026|work=UEFA.com|accessdate=11 August 2026}}</ref>

Paris Saint-Germain won the match 2–1 for their second UEFA Super Cup title.<ref name="summary">{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/02a8-215538a51719-2eeabf96b5c7-1000/ |title=Paris 2–1 Aston Villa: European champions win back-to-back Super Cups with Khvicha Kvaratskhelia and Désiré Doué goals |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=12 August 2026 |access-date=12 August 2026}}</ref>

